**Theorem 8.2 (metric and compact-ball bridge).** For the representation
quotient in Definition 1.1, the function in Definition 8.1 is independent
of representatives. If the representation is properly discontinuous as in
Definition 2.1, this function is a metric inducing the existing quotient
topology. If in addition \(X\) is proper, then for every \(x\in X\) and
\(r\in\mathbb R\), with \(\pi:X\to X/\rho\) the quotient projection,

\[
 \overline B_{d_\rho}([x],r)=\pi(\overline B_{d_X}(x,r)).
\]

Hence \((X/\rho,d_\rho)\) is proper. Freeness and compactness of the quotient
are not hypotheses.

